    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0789" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg695"/>

                <head>No. 439.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Manning.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 17,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your No. 84 has just reached this Department. The purport of my telegram of March
                    7 last has not been understood.</p>
                <p>Whether the persons rescued are or are not Mexicans, nothing can satisfy the
                    Government of the United States except the delivery to its authorities of the
                    prisoners who were forcibly taken from the Arizona officials.</p>
                <p>The alternative offered in my telegram before mentioned only concerned the
                    Mexicans Who effected the rescue.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
